  "commandAssertions": [
    "Fresh human proof occurs before the writer transaction. Server authority binds household, actor, action and resource; current grants are rechecked before receipt disclosure.",
    "First creation writes absent defaults, definition, first occurrence, receipt, audit and outbox together. Injected failures after actual definition or occurrence writes leave no task/default residue.",
    "Title-only creation produces active/available work; explicit draft produces draft work. Original text and exact enum/override values survive bounded canonical request encoding.",
    "Any non-inherited task-rule override requires current administrator task configuration, even if creation permission remains after role/source revocation and even on original-receipt replay.",
    "Assignment accepts at most 32 distinct active household members and explicit release. Invalid/inactive members, revoked authority and stale revisions cannot partially change work.",
    "A real two-thread exclusive claim has one winner; the loser cannot silently reassign. Claim derives only the actor as assignee and retains current policy/exception restrictions.",
    "Replay precedes state/revision preconditions after authorization. A historical successful claim cannot reassign work released and later claimed by another member.",
    "Actual offline restoration is tested with the production creation and claim commands, actual SQLite/retained receipts and fake current proof. Restored-away operations return original historical results without allocating IDs or applying work."
  ],
