  "executionAssertions": [
    "Progress transitions cannot complete work; assigned actors may start/block/unblock while publishing, cancel/skip and reopening require current task management.",
    "Completion authorization checks assignment, restricted self-attribution and on-behalf grants before receipt disclosure. New performances then resolve active local participants, actual required work and effective rule/policy snapshots inside SQLite.",
    "Performer eligibility is a new-work precondition. An original authorized receipt remains immutable after another participant is archived, but revoked actor/on-behalf/approval grants still block disclosure.",
    "The performed default accepts pending prerequisite approval; the approved alternative waits for a current approved/no-verification-needed cycle. Rejected or unfinished prerequisite/subtask work blocks both.",
    "Approval/rejection persists a decision without closing; reopening closes the current cycle and retains attribution, performed time and original policy. Old cycle selectors cannot change a later genuine cycle.",
    "Cycle/occurrence/receipt/audit/outbox writes roll back together under failure injection after actual SQLite cycle or occurrence writes for completion, verification and reopening.",
    "Real competing completions produce one cycle/source event. A real approval/reopen race produces one decision and a consistent scoped revisioned current-cycle pointer.",
    "Live-reference fences reject missing defaults/prerequisites and deliberately corrupted missing/one-sided cycle records. An explicit broken semantic-port fixture cannot inject a foreign household cycle; it is not evidence for physical FK enforcement.",
    "Actual offline activation restores the older state; production completion/verification/reopening replay returns historical original receipts without applying effects or allocating IDs.",
    "Exactly one source event retains full cycle identity, revision, performers, policy/time facts and explicitly unconfirmed consumer delivery. Reopen supplies the compensation/review cause while completed dependent facts remain untouched."
  ]
}
